      "message": "Sorry, I only just realized after the code submitted, but could this be a problem:\n```\n  TargetInfo\u0026 info() const {\n    if (!info_.has_value()) {\n      info_.emplace(this);\n    }\n    return *info_;\n  }\n```\n\n\nIf info is called in a multithreaded context, in theory it could be mutated by multiple threads at the same time. I think we might need to make it:\n```\n  TargetInfo\u0026 info() const {\n    DCHECK(info_.has_value())\n    return *info_;\n  }\n```\n\nAnd initialize it in the builder. Or maybe your initialization in OnResolvedWithoutChecks already makes this safe, but we should remove the emplace and replace it with a DCHECK instead?",
